---
import catalog from '../../data/releases.json';
const repo = 'https://github.com/jmping/Glassmacs';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><title>Glassmacs releases and stability</title><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg"/><style>
:root{font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color-scheme:light dark}body{margin:0;background:#f6f8fc;color:#182b42;line-height:1.65}header,main,footer{max-width:900px;margin:auto;padding:22px 26px}a{color:#25628c}h1{font-size:clamp(2.5rem,6vw,4rem);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.05em}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #dce5ef;border-radius:16px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.tag{font-weight:700;color:#25628c}code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}nav{display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{background:#101b2a;color:#ecf3fb}.card{background:#172638;border-color:#31455c}a,.tag{color:#8ec9f0}}
</style></head><body><header><nav><a href="/">Glassmacs</a><a href="/roadmap/">Roadmap</a><a href="/faq/">FAQ</a></nav></header><main><h1>Releases and stability</h1><p>Choose a build based on its documented maturity, not simply its date. No stable release is listed in this catalog. Keep backups; alpha builds are intended for testing.</p><p>Catalog reviewed {catalog.reviewed}. <a href={repo+'/releases'}>All GitHub releases</a> (including any newer publications).</p>
<h2>Published versions</h2>{catalog.releases.map(r=><article class="card"><div class="tag">{r.stage} · {r.date}</div><h3>{r.version}</h3><p>{r.summary}</p><p>{r.evidence}</p><p><a href={repo+'/releases/download/'+r.version+'/'+r.asset}>Download ZIP</a> · <a href={repo+'/releases/download/'+r.version+'/'+r.asset+'.sha256'}>Checksum</a> · <a href={repo+'/releases/tag/'+r.version}>Release notes and assets</a></p>{r.sha256 && <p>SHA-256: <code>{r.sha256}</code></p>}</article>)}
<h2>In validation — not downloadable</h2><article class="card"><div class="tag">{catalog.candidate.stage}</div><p>Application source: <a href={repo+'/commit/'+catalog.candidate.commit}><code>{catalog.candidate.commit.slice(0,7)}</code></a>.</p><p>{catalog.candidate.evidence}</p><p>{catalog.candidate.blockers}</p><p>No public DMG link until publication is authorized and source obligations are resolved.</p></article>
<h2>What stability labels mean</h2><dl><dt><strong>Development candidate</strong></dt><dd>Internal build; not necessarily available or installable.</dd><dt><strong>Validation prerelease</strong></dt><dd>Signed distribution artifact for targeted testing; limitations and unverified platforms explicitly listed.</dd><dt><strong>Alpha</strong></dt><dd>Experimental functionality; substantial changes and defects possible.</dd><dt><strong>Beta</strong></dt><dd>Core workflows and clean-machine installation accepted on advertised platforms; known limitations remain.</dd><dt><strong>Release candidate</strong></dt><dd>Feature scope frozen; final regression and distribution gates pending.</dd><dt><strong>Stable</strong></dt><dd>Declared acceptance gates met for supported platforms; not a guarantee of defect-free operation.</dd></dl><p>Signing and notarization are security/distribution checks, not evidence of functional stability. See the <a href="/roadmap/">roadmap</a> and <a href={repo+'/blob/main/docs/acceptance-matrix.md'}>acceptance matrix</a>.</p>
<h2>Installation and feedback</h2><p>Read the version-specific release notes. For ZIP builds, extract and move Glassmacs.app to Applications. For future DMGs, open the image and follow its installation instructions. Check the published checksum before installing, and do not bypass Gatekeeper if validation fails. Keep backups and report the version, macOS version, architecture and reproduction steps in <a href={repo+'/issues'}>GitHub issues</a>.</p></main><footer><a href="/">Home</a> · <a href="/provenance/">Documentation provenance</a></footer></body></html>
